.TH ROCKETSCIENCE 1
.SH NAME
rocketscience \- guided rocket game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/rocketscience
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I RocketScience
is Terry Davis's guided-rocket demo:
a rocket steered by proportional navigation with a servo-driven nozzle
chases a plane flying overhead.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
On start (and on every restart) a popup asks for the anti-spin
coefficient, chosen from an exponentially spaced menu between 0.1 and 10;
experimenting with it is the point of the demo.
Use the arrow keys and Enter, or click an entry, to choose.
Once chosen, any key blasts off.
The number printed at the top left is the estimated time to intercept.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B Up / Down
Move the popup cursor
.TP
.B Enter
In the popup, choose the highlighted coefficient;
in flight, restart (the coefficient is asked again)
.TP
.B "any key"
Blast off, once the coefficient is chosen
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/rocketscience.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR ode (2),
.IR tone (2),
